    {
      "sentence_id": 10,
      "text": "1. Learned counsel appearing for the litigants ad idem submit that the matter in issue is covered, by\nthe judgment of the Constitution Bench of the Hon'ble Apex Court, rendered in case titled as 'Indore\nDevelopment Authority Versus Manoharlal and others' Air 2020 Sc 1496, to which Slp (Civil) Nos.\n9036-9038 of 2016, has been assigned, and, the instant petition be permitted to be disposed of, as\nsuch.\n2.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 590,
      "end": 996,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Indore\nDevelopment Authority Versus Manoharlal and others' Air 2020 Sc 1496",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 786,
          "end": 861
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 11,
      "text": "In view of both contingencies, spelt therein, thus against attraction of the lapsing provisions to the acquired lands, and, as required under Section 24(2) of The Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land Acquisition, Rehabilitation and Resettlement Act, 2013, thus becoming complied with, therefore, there is no lapsing of the earlier drawn acquisition proceedings.\n3. Disposed of, as such.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 997,
      "end": 1399,
